⟦ certification_rubric | VSF-CERT-RUBRIC-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-17T07:29:21Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
// docs/spec_revision/design-sources/vsf-cert-rubric-v1/certification_rubric.vsm
// The rubric every document in docs/spec_revision is certified against.
// Scope: ALL of spec_revision, not boot/ alone. Established 2026-08-07 (rmw3).
// RELOCATED 2026-08-17 → design-sources/ (CLASSIFICATION-POLICY-PLAN S3):
// a certification INSTRUMENT — lives OUTSIDE system/ so it may name
// explicit paths (hard_rules.R_ref_resolution binds system/ only).

rubric(VSF-CERT-RUBRIC-v1) {

  scope: "
    The object of certification is system/ ONLY. Everything else under
    docs/spec_revision — revision_plan, census_docs, worklist_vsl,
    ledger/compression_ledger, this rubric — is META: the work's GUIDES, NOT the
    work. Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-07.
    // Certifying meta was scope creep and it showed: a D7 sweep over the
    // whole tree returned 41 findings inside a ledger that RECORDS
    // translation operations. A rule applied outside its object produces
    // findings that are true and useless.
    D7: every document in system/ is in English. ONE exception —
    covenant.vsm is bilingual BY DESIGN; its Spanish is the original, paired
    with EN. Gated by symbol_table.py --d7."

  authority: "
    Three anchors, in order. A document conflicting with one of them is
    NOT certified regardless of how well it scores elsewhere:
      1. covenant.vsm      — A0/A0.1, formal structure, channels, viability
      2. core_boot_primer  — axioms, notation, closure
      3. vsl_language      — alphabet, grammar, conventions
    Conflict BETWEEN anchors resolves against the KERNEL, then the papers.
    NOT by seniority, NOT by which document is more recent.
    // Precedent 2026-08-07: covenant's φ↑/φ↓ level indices contradicted
    // primer A1. Kernel (kernel.rs: child = self.level + 1) settled it —
    // covenant was wrong in BOTH copies, and its own prose already said so.
    // The covenant is the top anchor and was still the defective party."

  // ── MECHANICAL — gated, binary, ∄ judgement ─────────────────────────────
  mechanical: "
    header        ⟦ name | id | vsm-1.2.1 | date ⟧, EXACTLY 4 fields, line 1
    footer        ⟦ /name ⟧, same 4 fields, last line
    identity_path name in the header ≡ the file's own path segment
    vsm_version   @vsm 1.2 on the 2nd non-blank line
    encoding      UTF-8 ∧ NFC ∧ ¬BOM ∧ ¬invisible(NBSP, ZW*)
    no_emojis     six pictographic ranges forbidden; permitted ✓ ◐ ◯ ✗ ?
                  and the declared typographic set ✸ † ★ ▼
    glyph_closure ∀ glyph ∈ doc: g ∈ vsl_language.alphabet ∪ primer.notation
    separator     ▪ for lists in boot/ ; · stays multiplication everywhere
    prime         ′ in formulas only ; ' in prose only, never a prime
    minus         − (U+2212) for arithmetic ; - for identifiers and dates ;
                  – for ranges ; — for prose
    loop_class    bare Ln is ALWAYS a recursion level ; D4-Ln is the class ;
                  VSI-Ln is the coupling-protocol layer ; L(x) is Lyapunov
    gates         scripts/vsl/verify_encoding.py
                  scripts/vsl/verify_primer_closure.py
                  scripts/vsl/verify_boot_primer.py
                  scripts/state/verify_covenant_hash.py"

  // ── SUBSTANTIVE — read, NOT scripted ───────────────────────────────────────
  substantive: "
    vs_covenant     NOT contradicts A0/A0.1, the ⟨S1..S5⟩ @ E(L) structure, the
                    six channels, or viability as Ω-membership
    vs_primer       NOT contradicts A1..A11, the notation, or the channel
                    directions and level indices
    vs_vsl_language NOT contradicts the alphabet, the grammar, or the declared
                    conventions
    hard_rules      R_ref_resolution: ∀ doc ∈ system/, ∄ explicit path in the
                    body — symbolic @var bound in system/instance/vsf-instance-v1/instance.vsm
    internal_logic  read END TO END. ∄ self-contradiction, ∄ formula that
                    contradicts its own comment, ∄ claim whose verifier is
                    unnamed
    namespacing     ∀ identifier NOT in the canon: carries a DECLARED namespace.
                      extension of a canon item  → suffix:  A8.vOS, A12.vOS
                      unrelated taxonomy         → own prefix: DP1..DP5
                      citation/compliance verdict → the block says so
                    // Found 2026-08-07: vos_core_theory's session
                    // anti-patterns were numbered D1..D5, colliding with the
                    // canon's D1..D5 (viable_system, upward, downward,
                    // recursion_condition, LLM_constraint). Every duplicate
                    // sweep would report them as rival definitions, forever.
                    // The .vOS suffix pattern already existed in the SAME
                    // document, declared and correct — it just had not been
                    // applied to the rest.
    level_direction ∀ statement about recursion: CITE A1, NOT restate it. If it
                    must be restated, use NAMED ROLES — parent, child — NOT L±1.
                    // Found in THREE documents on 2026-08-07/08, independently:
                    //   vos_proofs §8      parent = child + 1
                    //   seven_ideas #4     "S1_{L,i} can be a complete VSM_{L−1}"
                    //   viable_compressor  RG flow L0 → L1 → L2 → L3, stations
                    //                      at the root, simplex at the leaves
                    // All three inherited it from prose restating A1 from
                    // memory. The primer's OWN arithmetic is correct — the
                    // defect is NOT the notation, it is the restatement. A named
                    // role cannot invert; an index can, and did, three times.
    cited_is_declared ∀ identifier CITED in system/ ∃ a declaration in
                    system/. A live document resting on an axiom the canon
                    does NOT carry is a foundation nobody can check.
                    // Reported by symbol_table --paths, NOT gated: the standing
                    // 20 (debt CITED-AXIOMS-NOT-ABSORBED) are a pass of real
                    // work, and a gate that blocks on a standing backlog is a
                    // gate that gets switched off.
                    // The question came from OUTSIDE our tooling: exporting
                    // the index to RDF and letting a graph engine ask it.
                    // ∄ gate of ours had asked, and three days of reading
                    // found ONE instance (Ax_SplitOperator) of twenty-three.

    ontology_trigger INTEGRATE OWL 2 RL reasoning WHEN a relational defect
                    RECURS after level_direction is in force.
                    // Measured 2026-08-09: a reasoner derives 3/3 of the
                    // relational defects this cycle found BY READING —
                    // recursion inversion, S3* as a tuple element, D6 —
                    // with 0 false positives, in the RL profile, in Python.
                    // NOT integrated now, deliberately: the class is already
                    // attacked by PREVENTION (level_direction says cite A1,
                    // NOT restate it), and prevention is cheaper than inference.
                    // The honest counter, recorded so it is NOT forgotten:
                    // prevention depends on compliance, detection does NOT.
                    // The FIRST recurrence proves prevention insufficient
                    // and pays for the reasoner. Benchmarks kept in scratch.

    duplication     ∃ duplicate formal statement ⟹ ONE of:
                      (a) deliberate and stated — covenant/vsl_language both
                          need the primer's axiom preamble, because the primer
                          is a self-contained agnostic boot loadable into a
                          chat agent with no other context
                      (b) @status historical_record — a dated record, kept
                          unedited, skipped by sweeps
                      (c) removed: the document CITES the canon, NOT restates it
                    // ∄ fourth option. An unstated duplicate is a divergence
                    // waiting to happen, and the cost lands on every future
                    // review, not on the commit that created it.
    // internal_logic is the criterion no gate can carry. Every gate in this
    // rubric passed the corpus while A5 mixed two namespaces three lines
    // apart, D6's level bound was inverted, and A14's formula contradicted
    // its own comment. Marking it ✓ REQUIRES having read the document."

  recertification: "
    A MECHANICAL edit DECERTIFIES the document until the touched sites are
    re-read. Passing the gates again is NOT enough.
    // 2026-08-07: 31 path→@var substitutions across the two anchors. Every
    // gate stayed green while one of them had turned a TYPE production,
    // `ref(@ref docs/spec/…)`, into `ref(@ref @dir_spec/…)` — two tokens
    // where the grammar wants one operand. Syntactically valid, semantically
    // incoherent, invisible to every checker. Found only by re-reading the
    // substitution sites."

  density: "
    VSL is a COMPRESSED notation. Prose in a spec passes every other axis —
    it parses, it closes, it encodes clean — and says in a paragraph what
    notation says in a line.
    target: prose ≤ 5% ▪ words/line ≤ 5.0    (boot/ measures 0% ▪ 4.2)
    gated by symbol_table.py --density
    // compression ≢ fewer lines. s5_policy_annex went 262 → 393 lines while
    // dropping 23% → 1% prose and 8.7 → 5.0 words/line: MORE lines, each
    // shorter and readable alone. Words fell 12%.

    TOKEN COST, measured 2026-08-07 (o200k_base) — byte ≢ token:
      → ∀ Ω ¬ ≤   1 token   (cheaper than their ASCII spellings)
      ∈ ∧          2 tokens  (dearer than ` in`, ` & `)
      ⟹ ⟦ ⟧        3 tokens  (⟹ is 3× the cost of →, same bytes)
    corpus system/ = 143k tok. operators 3.6% ▪ banners 2.1% ▪
    COMMENTS 28.5%. The volume is in comments, NOT in notation."

  deferred_pass: "
    AFTER the translation/compression sweep completes, evaluate the corpus as a
    WHOLE and prune comments. Agreed rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-07 — doing it earlier
    optimises a body that is still changing.
    PROTECT: forensic comments are only 1.9% of the corpus; the volume is
    EXPLANATORY comment, and that is what lets an external agent read the
    document with no other context — the primer's declared purpose. The prune
    must separate 'this explains the document' from 'this narrates how we got
    here'. Cutting by percentage would destroy the first to save the second."

  finding_disposition: "
    DOCUMENT finding  ⟹ resolved in the SAME pass. ∄ backlog.
    KERNEL finding    ⟹ recorded in place, BATCHED until system/ is fully
                        certified. Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-07.
    // two reasons, both structural: (a) the spec is still moving — aligning
    // the kernel to a document under certification chases a target; (b)
    // model≡reality is a BIJECTION, NOT a list: batching gives ONE
    // build → spec_boot → R4 deploy cycle instead of N.
    // This is NOT the backlog habit. A backlog is a finding that leaves the
    // document; these stay written where they were found, with their
    // evidence, and the batch is the last phase of the cycle."

  verdict: "
    CERTIFIED  ⟺ ∀ mechanical ∧ ∀ substantive
    ◐          ⟺ read partially — state which lines
    ¬CERTIFIED ⟺ ∃ one ✗, of any class
    // ∄ partial credit. A document with correct notation and an inverted
    // axiom is NOT certified."

  exceptions: "
    covenant.vsm  constitutional SEAL ⟦ VSF ✸ 2026 | Valparaíso, Chile ⟧
                  waives the FOOTER only. The identity header is required —
                  the covenant carries both. The seal is NOT a node watermark:
                  covenant §watermark declares that format as four fields and
                  required of NODES; the seal is two, deliberately.
                  Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-07.

    covenant.vsm  ALSO exempt from @status(doc) — a DEFERRAL, NOT a waiver. It
                  carries a pending 1.1 → 1.2 amendment and a SHA256 in the
                  covenant hash registry; its status line rides with rmw3's
                  covenant promotion, NOT with a tooling pass. Editing a
                  constitutional document to satisfy a gate written the same
                  day is the wrong order.
                  debt(COVENANT-STATUS-DEFERRED, class=doc, owner=rmw3,
                  gate=covenant_1_2) — the ONE document with ∄ declared
                  epistemic state, and it is the top anchor.
                  ∄ other exception. Declared here or it does NOT exist."
}

⟦ /certification_rubric ⟧
